          ":question/problem": "For $f(x,y,z)=x \\sqrt{4 y^{2} + 4 z^{2}}$, evaluate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}$ at the point $(-1,2,- \\frac{3}{2})$.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Differentiate with respect to $z$, holding $x$ and $y$ fixed. Use the constant multiple and chain rules, then substitute the coordinates. At this point the radicand is $25>0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=x\\cdot\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{4 y^{2} + 4 z^{2}}}\\cdot 8 z\\\\&=\\frac{4 x z}{\\sqrt{4 y^{2} + 4 z^{2}}}\\\\\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\big|_{(-1,2,- \\frac{3}{2})}&=\\frac{4\\left(- \\frac{3}{2}\\right)(-1)}{\\sqrt{25}}\\\\&=\\frac{6}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
